  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.15.1: Wasm bugfix - device-local managed arrays (`new T[N]` in a kernel, indexed in a loop) now compile correctly on the Wasm backend; previously they produced silently-wrong results (Wasm only; the other 5 backends were correct). Two stacked Wasm-backend causes: the backend ran no LowerArrays IR pass so `new T[]` reached codegen as un-lowered NewArray/LoadArrayElementAddress nodes (element address never computed -> hit address 0), and once lowered the local alloca was type-only-aliased onto a kernel's shared-memory buffer (clobbered across barriers). `LocalMemory.Allocate<T>` was never affected. Forks unchanged at 2.0.42. Full history: CHANGELOG.md at https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.ILGPU/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
  "repository": {
